Article 3 The People's Procuratorate may assign or engage persons who have expert appraisal qualifications or other persons who, after review by the People's Procuratorate, possess professional competence, to participate in case handling as persons with specialized knowledge.
No person shall participate in case handling as a person with specialized knowledge if such person falls under any of the following circumstances:
(1) having had the expert appraisal qualification cancelled, the expert appraiser registration revoked, or other practicing qualifications suspended, or having been punished by suspension from practice within the past three years, due to violation of professional ethics;
(2) having no civil capacity or only limited civil capacity;
(3) having violated the provisions of Articles 18 to 21 of these Provisions within the past three years;
(4) having participated in the handling of the present case as a case handler or in another capacity;
(5) other circumstances where it is inappropriate for such person to participate in case handling as a person with specialized knowledge.

Article 7 Where the People's Procuratorate needs to collect evidence in handling a criminal case, it may assign or engage a person with specialized knowledge to carry out the following tasks:
(1) conducting an inspection or examination under the auspices of the prosecutor;
(2) testing specialized issues that require expert appraisal but for which there is no statutory appraisal institution;
(3) other necessary tasks.

Article 8 When the People's Procuratorate, upon review for prosecution, discovers that the evidence material involving specialized issues falls under any of the following circumstances, it may assign or engage a person with specialized knowledge to conduct a review and issue a review opinion:
(1) having a significant impact on conviction and sentencing;
(2) having an irreconcilable conflict with other evidence;
(3) there are two or more appraisal opinions on the same specialized issue and the conclusions are inconsistent;
(4) the parties, defenders, or litigation agents have raised objections;
(5) other necessary circumstances.

Article 9 After the People's Court decides to hold a hearing, the People's Procuratorate may assign or engage a person with specialized knowledge to assist the public prosecutor in preparing for the following:
(1) mastering the circumstances of evidence material involving specialized issues;
(2) supplementing the specialized knowledge that may be involved in the trial;
(3) drafting a plan for interrogating the defendant and questioning witnesses, expert appraisers, and other persons with specialized knowledge;
(4) drafting a plan for presenting, playing, or demonstrating evidence material involving specialized issues;
(5) formulating a cross-examination plan;
(6) other necessary tasks.

Article 12 When the People's Procuratorate decides to file a public interest litigation case and investigates and collects evidence, it may, with respect to evidence material or professional issues involving specialized issues, assign or engage a person with specialized knowledge to assist in carrying out the following tasks:
(1) answering, explaining, or clarifying professional questions;
(2) evaluating or auditing the specialized issues involved in the case;
(3) rendering opinions on appraisal matters involving complex, difficult, or special technical issues;
(4) inspecting physical evidence or the scene under the auspices of the prosecutor;
(5) reviewing evidence material involving specialized issues in administrative law enforcement case files;
(6) other necessary tasks.

Article 14 Where the People's Procuratorate needs to assign or engage persons with specialized knowledge in the following case handling activities, these Provisions may apply:
(1) handling cases of complaints, petitions, state compensation, or state judicial assistance;
(2) handling cases of serious injury or death of persons under custody occurring in custodial facilities;
(3) handling supervisory cases in civil or administrative proceedings;
(4) deliberation and decision by the Procuratorial Committee on major cases and other major issues;
(5) other case handling activities requiring the assignment or engagement of persons with specialized knowledge.

Article 15 The People's Procuratorate shall provide the following necessary conditions for persons with specialized knowledge to participate in case handling:
(1) introducing the circumstances related to the specialized issues involved in the case;
(2) providing case file materials such as evidence involving specialized issues;
(3) specifying the issues for which assistance or opinions are required;
(4) other conditions necessary for persons with specialized knowledge to participate in case handling.
